keywords:
  - agentic AI
  - virtual screening
  - software verification
  - applicability domain
  - conformal prediction
  - natural products
  - adenosine A2A receptor
abstract: >-
  Code, contracts, deterministic evaluators, the seeded-defect benchmark and the
  verification evidence behind a study in which an agentic virtual-screening
  pipeline was run against the adenosine A2A receptor and the verification of
  the agent-written code is reported as a result rather than assumed. No
  compound reported is supported by any wet-laboratory assay.
references:
  - type: data
    title: LOTUS natural products database, v11 frozen snapshot
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19360665
    notes: >-
      CC BY 4.0. Structures and organism names under verification/ derive from
      it and attribution is required wherever they are reused.
  - type: article
    title: 'ChEMBL: towards direct deposition of bioassay data'
    doi: 10.1093/nar/gky1075
    notes: >-
      CC BY-SA 3.0. No ChEMBL records are deposited here, only aggregate
      statistics from models trained on them.
